# Criterion review: code-context-engineering AC-02

A rename/edit invalidates old entries and updates affected ones; oracle: controlled repository mutations.

APPROVED in the following evaluated scope: Synthetic declaration/import/call corpus; exact source bytes and generation; actual rename/edit of owned temporary files and absent executable; no Rust parser or working LSP client. Unchanged files reuse parsed declarations, with no repository-scale performance claim.

Observed: context_ac02_rename_edit: real rename then write invalidates the old hit/path/name, updates b.fixture/renamed at generation 2, and reparses zero files when bytes are unchanged.

Method: inspect the independent assertions and concrete implementation, execute commands captured in replay/receipt.json or environment.json/gui-02/result.json, and inspect their full logs. Expected values are independently specified fixture values; exit zero alone is insufficient. The original criterion and skill contracts are unchanged.

Consumer: tools/governance/consumers/models.rs; oracle: tools/governance/consumers/model_tests.rs. Broader contracts/exclusions: tools/governance/consumers/README.md. All prior envelopes are byte-preserved in previous/. This does not accept a production Ox subsystem or infer new agent effectiveness.
